{"id":"u-b50c71b6-5a99-4d98-a454-a8fbe0e536d0","src":"community","title":"Full Body Hypertrophy - 3 Days a Week","author":"Mark L.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/qLFr9Y-fullbodyhypertrophy12weekboostcampimport","desc":"This 12-week program is designed for lifters who already have some gym experience and want to build more muscle while continuing to get stronger.\n\nTraining is performed three days per week using full-body workouts, with each session typically lasting about 40–50 minutes. The program combines barbells, dumbbells, cables, and machines to provide enough variety to keep training fresh without turning each workout into a random collection of exercises.\n\nThe main focus is hypertrophy, with most training performed in productive moderate-rep ranges, while heavier compound work is retained to continue building strength. Squats, conventional deadlifts, presses, rows, pulldowns, and other proven movements form the foundation, supported by targeted work for shoulders, arms, hamstrings, calves, and upper back.\n\nExercise selection changes throughout the 12 weeks, but the major movement patterns remain consistent enough to allow measurable progression. Planned deload weeks help manage fatigue, and the final weeks gradually increase training intensity without requiring maximal lifts or training to failure.\n\nThis program is ideal for someone who enjoys full-body training, wants variety from workout to workout, prefers resistance training over cardio-focused sessions, and wants to build muscle steadily while allowing body composition to improve over time.","level":["Novice"],"goals":["Strength","Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":40,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-09-26T15:33:00.387Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Hypertrophy Base A — Squat & Row","Hypertrophy Base B — Hack & Shoulders","Hypertrophy Base C — Deadlift & Chest"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"Con